          "text": "is an appropriate compensatory response; thus, phlebotomy may be dangerous; if indicated, remove blood at a lower volume (5 mL/kg). A higher PCV (60–65%) may be necessary to sustain life until the cause of hypoxemia can be corrected.",
          "pdf_page": 545,
          "printed_page": 463,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Polycythemia vera—phlebotomy (20 mL/kg) and hydroxyurea; frequency of bleeding and dosage adjusted to maintain a PCV of 55% in dogs and 45% in cats.",
          "pdf_page": 545,
          "printed_page": 463,
          "column": 1
        }
      ],
      "subsections": {
        "GENERAL": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "GENERAL",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE",
          "canonical_heading": "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "leiomyosarcoma), hyperadrenocorticism, hyperthyroidism, hyperandrogenism.",
              "pdf_page": 544,
              "printed_page": 462,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Relative—rehydration with IV fluids",
              "pdf_page": 544,
              "printed_page": 462,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Secondary absolute caused by inappropriate appropriate for primary cause; assessment of EPO or darbepoetin administration in renal function, gastrointestinal system, animals undergoing therapy for anemia. acid-base status, and electrolyte balance; if not hemoconcentrated, allow patient to calm down.",
              "pdf_page": 544,
              "printed_page": 462,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Absolute—phlebotomy recommended (20 mL/kg over 1 to several days) to reduce",
              "pdf_page": 544,
              "printed_page": 462,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "NURSING CARE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "NURSING CARE",
          "canonical_heading": "NURSING CARE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Oxygen therapy may be indicated for patients with cyanosis, hypoxemia, cardiopulmonary disease, or weakness following phlebotomy.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "ACTIVITY": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "ACTIVITY",
          "canonical_heading": "ACTIVITY",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Excessive exercise should be avoided.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "DIET": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIET",
          "canonical_heading": "DIET",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Normal diet, free-choice water.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "CLIENT EDUCATION": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "canonical_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Patients need to be observed at home for changes in activity, difficulty breathing, or bleeding.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Patients treated with EPO for anemia must have PCV rechecked and dose adjusted at regular intervals.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "If surgery is necessary, preoperative phlebotomy and close monitoring of oxygenation and vital parameters may be necessary. Postoperatively, monitor for bleeding or thrombosis.",
              "pdf_page": 545,
              "printed_page": 463,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "MEDICAL": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "MEDICAL",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
